	abstract = {Large Language Models speed up software development but often produce flawed, non-production-ready code resulting in a controversy over their use. Existing AI coding tools lack transparency, confidence scores, and clear explanations. We present eXAI-CodeDebug, an explainable code analysis framework that combines static analysis with LLM-based detection to ensure production-quality code. It provides dual confidence scores, separately measuring certainty for detected issues and proposed fixes—plus detailed explanations and one-click automated corrections. The system covers seven issue categories, including hallucinations and security vulnerabilities, with customizable filters and thresholds. On 48 seeded issues, it achieves 100% precision and recall for Security and Hallucination, 85.7% F1 Score for Bug Detection, Quality, and Trustworthiness, and 69% Quick Fix success. Analysis averages 12.5 seconds per file and reduces debugging time from 6–23 minutes to under 2 seconds per issue. © 1999-2011 IEEE.},
